          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.1.1 A simple pendulum"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.113,
            0.367,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A simple pendulum consists of a small metallic ball (called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "bob",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the pendulum) suspended from a rigid support by a long thread as shown in Fig. 8.7a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.115,
            0.723,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We did an activity in the chapter ‘Measurement of Length and Motion’ in the Grade 6 Science textbook Curiosity, where we observed the oscillatory motion of an eraser hung with a thread. Is the pendulum similar to that?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
