              "bbox": [
                0.538,
                0.436,
                0.566,
                0.453
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(b)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.321,
                0.461,
                0.546,
                0.479
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 8.7: A simple pendulum"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.484,
            0.745,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The pendulum at rest is in its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "mean position",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". When the bob of the pendulum is moved slightly to one side and released, it starts oscillatory motion. Its motion is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "periodic",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in nature because it repeats its path after a fixed interval of time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.56,
            0.744,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The pendulum is said to have completed "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "one oscillation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " when its bob, starting from its mean position O, moves to extreme position A, changes direction and moves to another extreme position B, changes direction and comes back to O (Fig. 8.7b). The pendulum also completes one oscillation when its bob moves from one extreme position A to another extreme position B and comes back to A. The time taken by the pendulum to complete one oscillation is called its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "time period",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Let us now set up a pendulum and measure its time period."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.733,
            0.44,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 8.2: Let us experiment",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.77,
            0.743,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Collect a piece of string around 150 cm long, a heavy metal ball with hook/ a stone (bob), a stopwatch/ watch, and a ruler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.813,
            0.505,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Tie the bob at one end of the string."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.837,
            0.743,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Fix the other end of the string to a rigid support such that the length of the string in between support and bob is around 100 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.898,
            0.743,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Wait for the bob to come to rest. Your pendulum is now ready."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
